{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the harsh sunlight surprisingly pixelated. He sat up in bed, a strange, blocky texture beneath his fingers. His bedroom, usually cluttered with books and half-finished projects, was rendered in a vibrant, almost cartoonish style. A health bar floated above his head, displaying a disconcerting green glow. He reached out, tentatively touching his arm – the skin felt… artificial. A notification popped up in his vision: \"Welcome, Arthur! You are now a player in 'Aethelgard: Realm of Eldoria'. Level 1 achieved. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin Caves.\" Panic seized him. This wasn't a dream; it was something far more bizarre. He glanced at his reflection in the mirrored wardrobe, noticing his clothes were now roughspun tunic and leather trousers, a far cry from his usual jeans and t-shirt.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of his room and into a world teeming with fantastical creatures. A squirrel with oversized ears chattered at him from a low-hanging branch, its movements jerky and pre-programmed. A knight in shining armor, looking equally bewildered, nearly collided with him. \"By the Light! Who are you?\" the knight exclaimed, his voice a synthesized baritone. Arthur stammered, trying to explain his predicament, but the words felt clumsy, inadequate. He was trapped in a game, a character in someone else’s adventure. The Sunstone quest seemed less like a challenge and more like an unavoidable directive. He sighed, the weight of virtual destiny settling heavily on his shoulders. He had a feeling this was going to be a very long day.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4622840881347656}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0001805857609724626}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.07861142605543137}, {"token": "▁harsh", "logprob": -1.166972279548645}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logpro